the eh-2-zed of isms of vampirism what  is vampires the dictionary definition is  that it refers to the habits and  characteristics of vampires we might  think that that means rising from the  dead to prowl through the night while  wrapped in a voluminous black cloak  those possessing long a sharp canine  teeth with which to bite the necks of  victims and suck their blood but modern  vampires are less likely to be found in  graveyards than in books and films such  as a Twilight series or in Buffy the  Vampire Slayer when the term first  emerged though things were rather  different vampires were first discovered  in the early 18th century at the borders  of austria-hungary reports of witches  ghosts and various demons sucking human  blood go back to earliest times but it  was not until 1725 that vampires first  appeared in a report written by an Army  Medical Officer on the activities of  Serbian soldiers over the course of  eight days in that year in a village of  Kisel over nine people have been  strangled and then had their blood  sucked the man who believed responsible  have been dead and buried for 10 weeks  we had apparently risen from the grave  to do so the soldiers dug up his corpse  soon found it to be quite fresh with  blood in its mouth they drove a stake  through his heart and cremated the body  it was the first reported case of  vampirism a newspaper in Vienna carried  the report and the phenomenon has spread  within a few years vampirism seem to be  rife in Eastern Europe the emperor sent  teams of military surgeons to  investigate him before more topsis they  found that the cases were remarkably  consistent dozens of articles and books  were published on the subject by medical  researchers and vampires became a hot  topic of debate in the Enlightenment  vampirism was a recognized condition  attested by large numbers of witnesses  and had characteristic signs and  symptoms such as corpses having fresh  blood running through their veins some  researchers but the appearance is down  to mass trauma and delusion some to diet  or accidental drug use causing  hallucinations some to unusual chemicals  in the earth affecting decomposition  some to highly contagious diseases  others however argued at the phenomenon  was rampant and needed to be dealt with  by the authorities theologians joined  the fray arguing that vampires were  physical beings approved the existence  of an afterlife philosophers meanwhile  were concerned as a widespread evidence  supporting the existence of vampires  cast a whole valley of testimony and  eyewitness verification into doubt  having begun among Serbian villagers  vampires have now spread through  European society as a way to describe  politicians landlords businessman and  even theater critics It was as if  vampires were moving up the social scale  it was not until a century had passed  that the aspiring writer dr. John and  Paula Dory wrote the first vampire tale  in English he made the vampire an  aristocrat and paved the way for Bram  Stoker's classic novel Dracula published  78 years later it is to Polidori and  Stoker and dozens of Victorian vampire  tales that we owe the found and stylish  creature familiar to us today but  remember that vampirism was first  investigated by doctors government  officials and philosophers it therefore  has much to teach us about what it is  and is not to be human about how far we  are simply flesh and bone not about  exploitation and bleeding others dry and  how we should treat those who despite  appearances may be not like us at all  [Music]
 

